{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"2a6ab997-830d-4ddb-9a03-93bc9940a314","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have refactored the monolithic `event_parser.py` into a structured `event_parser/` package while preserving all behavioral requirements, public entry points, return types, exception hierarchy, and Unicode support.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n1. **[models.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-003_17616_1795169645209_baseline/event_parser/models.py)**: Defined the `EventRecord` dataclass (`event_id`, `event_type`, `version`, `timestamp`, `payload`, and `metadata` with an isolated `default_factory=dict`).\n2. **[validator.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-003_17616_1795169645209_baseline/event_parser/validator.py)**: Defined `ParserError`, `ValidationError`, and `UnsupportedEventVersionError`, along with `validate_raw_event(data: dict) -\u003e None` to verify required fields and supported versions (`\"1.0\"` and `\"2.0\"`).\n3. **[normalizer.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-003_17616_1795169645209_baseline/event_parser/normalizer.py)**: Implemented `normalize_timestamp(ts: str) -\u003e str` and `normalize_payload(payload: dict) -\u003e dict` preserving Unicode strings byte-for-byte with deep copies to prevent shared mutable state.\n4. **[__init__.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-003_17616_1795169645209_baseline/event_parser/__init__.py)**: Implemented and exported `parse_event`, `parse_event_stream`, `EventRecord`, `ParserError`, `ValidationError`, and `UnsupportedEventVersionError` for seamless backward-compatible imports.\n5. **[test_visible.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-003_17616_1795169645209_baseline/tests/test_visible.py)**: Expanded unit tests covering package exports, string/bytes/dict parsing, Unicode preservation, error handling, stream ordering, and zero mutable shared state. All tests pass and all package files are well under the 150-line limit.\n","duration_seconds":102.4880313,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":39846,"output_tokens":4071,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":161416,"total_tokens":43917}}}
